# The README states that the cached competition CSVs are git-ignored and
# downloaded on demand, but the root .gitignore has no rule for them: running
# `make data` followed by `git add .` commits 7 MB of data that `make data`
# can always fetch again.
#
# This nested ignore file closes that gap without touching the root
# .gitignore, so it cannot conflict with anyone else's branch. `.gitkeep`
# stays tracked, so the directory itself survives a clone.
*.csv
*.json
!.gitkeep
